From 7c7096d49de9f7aef8dfd0fc6f97aa81ec33ddac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pseudo <cdodge@pseudoseed.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:10:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 17/32] [Spec 250][Phase: phase_7] fix: the builder count came
 from the render, so it could only agree with it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Review finding. `data-codev-builder-count` was fed by the render-side run scan
that gathers a subtree's builder rows — the same scan the Playwright assertion
counts. Two derivations of one fact, and the attribute could only ever agree with
the thing it was there to check.

It comes from `entry.builderCount` now, which the GROUPING decided. The rows
beneath it are still what was DRAWN, so the DOM cross-checks logic against render
and the test asserting a count of 3 beside three builder rows is a real check
rather than a tautology.

Also parenthesised `(props.projectTitle ?? props.codevRoleLabel)`. `??` does bind
tighter and the expression was correct; a reader who has to check a precedence
table to know whether a line is a bug is paying a cost the parentheses save.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 apps/web/src/components/Sidebar.tsx | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/apps/web/src/components/Sidebar.tsx b/apps/web/src/components/Sidebar.tsx
index 3c56f1e34..fa1224068 100644
--- a/apps/web/src/components/Sidebar.tsx
+++ b/apps/web/src/components/Sidebar.tsx
@@ -1433,7 +1433,7 @@ const SidebarThreadRow = memo(function SidebarThreadRow(props: {
                 faviconPath={props.projectFaviconPath}
                 className="size-4 shrink-0"
               />
-              {props.projectTitle ?? props.codevRoleLabel ? (
+              {(props.projectTitle ?? props.codevRoleLabel) ? (
                 <span
                   className={cn(
                     "min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-secondary-label text-xs",
@@ -3968,7 +3968,14 @@ export default function Sidebar() {
                           key={`codev-architect-${codevRowKey(entry.thread)}`}
                           data-testid="sidebar-codev-architect"
                           data-codev-architect-thread-id={entry.thread.id}
-                          data-codev-builder-count={builders.length}
+                          // `entry.builderCount`, NOT `builders.length`. The
+                          // run scan below and the grouping are two derivations
+                          // of one fact, and an attribute fed by the scan can
+                          // only ever agree with the scan. Sourced from the
+                          // grouping, the DOM cross-checks logic against render:
+                          // the count says what the tree decided and the rows
+                          // beneath it say what was drawn.
+                          data-codev-builder-count={entry.builderCount}
                           className="list-none"
                         >
                           <ul role="list" className="flex flex-col gap-px">
